<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-RTZ-CRA sees potential for copper price fall.</title>
<headline>RTRS-RTZ-CRA sees potential for copper price fall.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>RTZ Corp Plc-CRA Ltd chief executive Robert Wilson said on Thursday it was possible that copper prices could fall a further 20 percent or more.</p>
<p>&quot;If you mean lower by 20 percent or more that is possible,&quot; Wilson said from London during a televised briefing after the group announced its half year results. &quot;I don't say that it is likely but it certainly is possible,&quot; Wilson said.</p>
<p>He said he doubted whether the slump in the copper price would last for a year, with a matter of months more likely.  </p>
<p>Wilson said the copper market was entering a period of over-supply but with consumption increasing he said he believed the duration of the over supply period would be shorter than some forecasters have predicted.</p>
</text>
